meta {
  name: S02 Drogon Seed Upload EPC
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/dataspaces/{{drogonSeedId}}/epc/upload?autoIngest=true
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  autoIngest: true
}

headers {
  data-partition-id: {{data-partition-id}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  epc: @file(../data/Demo_Drogon.epc)
}

docs {
  Drogon SELF-SEED (2/6). Uploads the Drogon EPC (Demo_Drogon.epc, 840 KB -
  the RESQML XML objects: grid, wells, property headers) into the fresh dataspace
  via POST /dataspaces/{ds}/epc/upload?autoIngest=true. EPC-ONLY on purpose (the
  H5 is intentionally omitted here - see the multipart note below). This makes the
  suite upgrade-proof and CI-portable: no pre-seeded space required. The object
  reads (S04/S05) and validate (S03) light up once /epc/upload is deployed; the
  grid ARRAY bytes live in the H5 and are exercised via Newman/Postman instead,
  which streams epc+h5 without the Bruno limitation below.

  NOTE: /epc/upload is a limited-deployment endpoint. On the CURRENT preship
  (pre-M27 client) it returns 404 and this test tolerates that (stays green). Once
  preship is upgraded to this M27 (~/rddms) client the upload succeeds and the
  downstream reads (S04/S05) and validate (S03) light up automatically.

  Bruno resolves @file() relative to the collection root (bruno/), so the path is
  ../data/Demo_Drogon.epc. For remote CI runs this fixture must be staged for the
  runner (it is git-ignored locally).

  IMPORTANT - EPC-ONLY (single file part) and NO tests/script blocks on purpose.
  The Bruno CLI (@usebruno/cli, quickjs marshalling) CRASHES on a multipart body
  with 2+ file parts whenever any NON-LAST part is more than a few KB - the 840 KB
  epc as the non-last part triggers it regardless of the H5 size, and it fires even
  with no user script (implicit post-response marshalling). So Bruno uploads are
  kept epc-only here; the full epc+h5 array round-trip is done under Newman/Postman.
  Verification is done downstream by S03 (validate), S04 (list resources) and S05
  (object content), which inspect server state rather than the request body.
}
